[00:00.000] 作曲 : Robert Pollard
[00:14.542] Well, if it's alright, it's already used
[00:21.763] I took a long drive and came back abused
[00:28.872] Don't think they see me, don't watch what they say
[00:35.721] Because I'm 81, I get confused every day
[00:41.007]
[00:44.625] And we may know no higher ceiling
[00:51.601] With any stained glass reflection
[00:58.758] I'm not supposed to be climbing ladders
[01:02.831]
[01:11.156] And I don't care about the clothes that I wear
[01:18.121] I'm not concerned and I cut my own hair
[01:25.097] I'll just go on and be dressed as the fool
[01:32.140] 'Cause I'm too old to pretend I still look cool
[01:37.328]
[01:40.905] I listened well and I went west, young man
[01:47.828] I took the name with it, the last stand
[01:54.902] And there are now no squares in Circleville
